{%- comment -%}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE TO DEVELOPERS: welcome to Impact theme! We hope that you will enjoy editing this theme as much as we did for
  developing it. We have put a lot of work to make this theme as developer friendly as possible by offering you
  hooks to integrate into critical parts of the theme. You will find the complete technical documentation (including
  all events, dependencies...) in the "documentation.txt" file, located in the Assets folder.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

<!doctype html>

<html class="no-js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}" dir="{% render 'direction' %}">
  <head>
	{%- comment -%}
	  Leftover from the uninstalled AVADA SEO Suite app, removed on 21/07/2026.

	  snippets/avada-seo.liquid includes avada-seo-site, avada-seo-structured, avada-seo-redirect and
	  avada-seo-local-business, none of which exist any more. Its own `unless contains 'Liquid error'` guard therefore
	  discarded the whole capture, so the block emitted nothing on every page: verified on the live HTML, the two
	  AVADA comment markers had only whitespace between them. All it still cost was four failed snippet lookups per
	  page render.

	  The orphan files left behind are snippets/avada-seo*.liquid, snippets/avada-defer-css.liquid and
	  templates/search.avada-seo.liquid. They are inert now that nothing includes them; delete them once it is
	  confirmed the app will not be reinstalled. SEO output today comes from the theme itself, plus SEOAnt.
	{%- endcomment -%}<!-- SEOAnt Speed Up Script -->{%- if shop.metafields.seoantAppSiteSpeedUpV2.switch == 1 -%}{% include 'SEOAnt-SpeedUp' %}{%- endif -%}<!-- /SEOAnt Speed Up Script -->
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.header_background }}">

    {%- comment -%}
      Custom vcollect: the free gift product must stay ACTIVE and published so /cart/update.js can add it to the cart
      (see snippets/gift-tiers-bar.liquid), which rules out an admin URL redirect: those only fire on 404 pages. Its
      product page therefore redirects to the homepage from the theme. Keyed on the 'cadeau-offert' tag like the cart
      gift lock, so adding another gift product needs no code change. The meta refresh covers no-JS visitors and is
      treated by Google as a redirect; noindex keeps the page out of the index either way.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if request.page_type == 'product' and product.tags contains 'cadeau-offert' -%}
      <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
      <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ routes.root_url }}">
      <script>window.location.replace({{ routes.root_url | json }});</script>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Custom vcollect (SEO audit 14/08/2026): tag-filtered collection URLs (/collections/handle/tag) are live,
      self-canonical duplicates of their base collection: 52 collections x 69 product tags is a latent pool of
      ~3,500 crawlable near-duplicates that robots.txt does not cover (a robots.txt.liquid override was tried on
      31/07 and rolled back: it loses the agentic header and the Allow rules). Same treatment for /search result
      pages, unbounded by nature. noindex,follow keeps the links crawlable so no equity is stranded, while the
      pages themselves stay out of the index.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if request.page_type == 'collection' and current_tags != blank -%}
      <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
    {%- elsif request.page_type == 'search' -%}
      <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Custom vcollect: give the homepage a title that contains what people search for.

      Shopify falls back to the shop name when the homepage title field in Online Store > Preferences is left empty,
      which shipped a <title> of exactly "VCOLLECT". No product word, no category word, so the homepage could not
      compete on anything but the brand itself, and Search Console confirmed it: every non-brand query landed
      elsewhere on the site.

      The override only applies while that admin field is still empty. Fill it in the admin and it wins again, so
      nobody has to come back and edit this file to change the wording.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign seo_title = page_title -%}
    {%- assign seo_description = page_description -%}

    {%- if request.page_type == 'index' and page_title == shop.name -%}
      {%- assign seo_title = 'VCOLLECT - Boutique Pokémon : displays, boosters et coffrets' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Custom vcollect: /collections/all is generated by Shopify without an admin record, so its SEO fields cannot be
      set anywhere in the admin. It shipped a <title> of exactly "Produits" and no meta description, and Search
      Console measured the result: 3 490 impressions for 40 clicks over the 28 days to 09/08/2026. The override
      steps aside as soon as a real "all" collection with its own SEO description exists in the admin.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if request.page_type == 'collection' and collection.handle == 'all' and seo_description == blank -%}
      {%- assign seo_title = 'Tous les produits Pokémon : displays, boosters et coffrets' -%}
      {%- assign seo_description = 'Tout le catalogue VCOLLECT sur une seule page : displays japonais et chinois, boosters, coffrets, ETB et accessoires de protection, scellés et 100 % authentiques.' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <title>{% if seo_title == blank %}{{ shop.name }}{% else %}{{ seo_title }}{% if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; {{ 'general.page' | t: page: current_page }}{% endif %}{% endif %}</title>

    {%- if seo_description != blank -%}
      <meta name="description" content="{{ seo_description | escape }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

    {%- comment -%}
      Impact core override: favicon and touch icons, resolved from theme settings.

      Google's requirements, read on developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/favicon-in-search on 30/07/2026: the
      icon must be square, at least 8x8px, and larger than 48x48px is recommended. rel="icon", rel="shortcut icon" and
      rel="apple-touch-icon" are all accepted, so the single rel="shortcut icon" Impact shipped was already a valid
      declaration. There is NO "multiple of 48" rule: an earlier version of this comment claimed there was.

      rel="icon" is added because it is the form defined by the HTML standard, which browsers and every other consumer
      read first: relying on the historical alias alone works for Google and works less well everywhere else. Both 48
      and 96 are emitted so the browser tab and the search result each get an exact-size file rather than a downscale,
      and height is passed alongside width so a non-square source is cropped square rather than declared square while
      being served oblong.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="48x48" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 48, height: 48 }}">
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="96x96" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 96, height: 96 }}">
      <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
      {%- comment -%} Kept for the older browsers that only look at this one. {%- endcomment -%}
      <link rel="shortcut icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 96, height: 96 }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}Few prefetch to increase performance on commonly used third-parties{%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.shopifycdn.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://productreviews.shopifycdn.com">

    {%- unless settings.heading_font.system? -%}
      <link rel="preload" href="{{ settings.heading_font | font_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    {%- endunless -%}

    {%- unless settings.text_font.system? -%}
      <link rel="preload" href="{{ settings.text_font | font_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    {%- endunless -%}

    {%- render 'social-meta-tags' -%}
    {%- render 'microdata-schema' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Custom (not Impact): the site-wide entity graph (Organization + WebSite, plus the page-level node for collections
      and pages). Rendered on every page, unlike the resource markup of 'microdata-schema'. See that snippet's tail for
      why the two are separate.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- render 'structured-data' -%}
    {%- render 'css-variables' -%}
    {%- render 'js-variables' -%}

    <script type="module" src="{{ 'vendor.min.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'sections.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

    {%- comment -%}
      Custom (not Impact): gift tiers, replacing the Monster Cart Upsell app.
      Loaded as a module so it defers like the theme's own scripts.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'custom-gift-tiers.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

    {%- comment -%}
      Custom (not Impact): reopens the right waitlist drawer with its
      confirmation after the native signup submission returns to the collection.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'custom-waitlist.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

    {{ content_for_header }}

    {{- 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true -}}

    {%- comment -%}
      Custom (not Impact): carousel edge fade and sticky product gallery.
      Loaded after theme.css so it overrides without needing !important.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {{- 'custom-vcollect.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag -}}
  </head>

  <body class="template-{{ request.page_type | handleize }} {% if settings.show_page_transition %}page-transition{% endif %} {% if settings.zoom_image_on_hover %}zoom-image--enabled{% endif %}">
    {%- render 'shadow-dom-templates' -%}

    <a href="#main" class="skip-to-content sr-only">{{ 'general.accessibility.skip_to_content' | t }}</a>

    {%- if request.page_type != 'password' -%}
      {%- sections 'header-group' -%}
      {%- sections 'overlay-group' -%}

      {%- if settings.cart_type == 'popover' -%}
        <cart-notification-drawer open-from="bottom" class="quick-buy-drawer drawer"></cart-notification-drawer>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if request.page_type == 'customers/account' or request.page_type == 'customers/order' or request.page_type == 'customers/addresses' -%}
      {%- section 'account-banner' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <main role="main" id="main" class="anchor">
      {%- comment -%}
      Custom (not Impact): breadcrumb on every page. Rendered here rather than inside each main-* section so a future
      Impact update has nothing to conflict with. See snippets/breadcrumb.liquid for the transparent-header caveat.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'breadcrumb' -%}

      {{ content_for_layout }}

      {%- comment -%}
      IMPLEMENTATION NOTE: due to the very complex logic of margin/padding collapsing in Impact, the footer group is
      added into the main element to ensure that dynamic sections added into the footer group are properly laid out.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if request.page_type != 'password' -%}
        {%- sections 'footer-group' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </main>

    {%- comment -%}
    Impact core override: policy pages (/policies/*) are rendered by Shopify from
    Settings > Policies. Those bodies were rewritten to VCOLLECT on 20/07/2026,
    but two sources still emit the legacy brand and cannot be fixed there:
      - the privacy policy is auto-generated by Shopify from the store email
        (Settings > General > store contact details), which belongs to the owner;
      - Judge.me injects its configured reply name into review widgets.
    Keep this client-side rebrand until both are settled at the source.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if request.path contains '/policies/' -%}
      <script>
        (() => {
          /**
           * Rewrite the legacy brand out of a string, while preserving the contact address.
           * The brand is written "VCOLLECT" (decision of 30/07/2026). It must stay in sync with the store name in
           * Settings > General: while that setting reads "Vcollect", shop.name feeds og:site_name and the structured
           * data with a different casing than the text below, which is what stops a search engine from consolidating
           * one entity.
           * The address deliberately stays pokeseller14@gmail.com (decision of 28/07/2026, reconfirmed on 30/07/2026:
           * the contact@vcollect.fr mailbox does not receive mail yet). Because it contains the brand name, it is
           * tokenised before the brand replaces run and restored after, otherwise it would become VCOLLECT@gmail.com.
           * @param {string} value - Raw text or href, as authored in the policy source
           * @returns {string} The same text under the current brand, contact address untouched
           */
          const rebrand = (value) =>
            value
              .replace(/pokeseller\s*14\s*@gmail\.com/gi, '@@contact-email@@')
              .replace(/pokeseller\s*14/gi, 'Vcollect')
              .replace(/pokeseller/gi, 'Vcollect')
              .replace(/@@contact-email@@/g, 'pokeseller14@gmail.com');

          /**
           * Walk the rendered policy body and rebrand every text node and every link that still names the old shop.
           * SCRIPT/STYLE/NOSCRIPT are skipped: app configs (Judge.me and friends) embed JSON there.
           * @returns {void}
           */
          const clean = () => {
            const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT, {
              acceptNode: (node) =>
                /^(SCRIPT|STYLE|NOSCRIPT)$/.test(node.parentNode.nodeName)
                  ? NodeFilter.FILTER_REJECT
                  : NodeFilter.FILTER_ACCEPT,
            });
            let node;
            while ((node = walker.nextNode())) {
              if (/pokeseller/i.test(node.nodeValue)) node.nodeValue = rebrand(node.nodeValue);
            }
            document.querySelectorAll('a[href*="okeseller" i]').forEach((link) => {
              link.setAttribute('href', rebrand(link.getAttribute('href')));
            });
          };

          document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', clean);
          /* App widgets inject their markup after load, so run once more when they settle */
          window.addEventListener('load', () => setTimeout(clean, 1500));
        })();
      </script>
    {%- endif -%}
  </body>
</html>